🔵 Blue Team Tools

Blue Team focuses on defending systems, detecting attacks, and responding to security incidents. It uses various tools to monitor networks, analyze threats, and strengthen security.

Wireshark: Used for analyzing network traffic to detect suspicious or malicious activity in real time.
Splunk: A powerful SIEM tool used to collect, search, and analyze log data from different systems for threat detection.
Suricata: An intrusion detection and prevention system (IDS/IPS) used to monitor network traffic and detect attacks.
ELK Stack (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana): Used for log management, data analysis, and creating visual dashboards for security monitoring.
OSSEC: A host-based intrusion detection system (HIDS) used to monitor system logs, file integrity, and detect unauthorized changes.

These tools help security teams detect attacks early, respond to incidents, and protect systems from ongoing threats.
